world-keyboard-windows (0.0.1~proto7) noble; urgency=medium

  * 44 more layouts, where Windows wins over the Linux layout of the same
    language (which stays next to it, unchanged): Russian (and
    Typewriter), Belarusian, Kazakh, Kyrgyz, Uzbek (Cyrillic), Bulgarian
    (Typewriter, Phonetic Traditional), Macedonian (2), Mongolian (4),
    Armenian (3), Georgian (5), Thai (4), Syriac (2), Pashto, Nepali,
    Dhivehi (2), US Dvorak (3), Ogham, Old Italic, N'Ko (3), Osmanya,
    Sora, Lisu and New Tai Lue. 111 in total. Not released.
  * Right Alt is AltGr in those of them that have AltGr characters on
    Windows (for example AltGr+8 gives the rouble sign in Russian).
  * Georgian: Caps Lock gives small letters as on Windows, also with
    newer libxkbcommon (which gives capitals on Linux's own Georgian).

 -- @MAINTAINER@  Thu, 05 Nov 2026 21:00:00 +0000

